manipulation('repeated-discount-amount',2,'A $60 item is reduced by 10%, then reduced by another $6. What is its final price in dollars?','42|48|50|54','48','60*9/10-6','A 10% reduction removes $6, leaving $54. The additional $6 reduction leaves $48.','A dollar reduction and a percentage reduction are different operations.')
manipulation('weighted-mean',3,'Two quiz scores average 14 points. A third score raises the average of all three to 16. What is the third score?','16|18|20|22','20','3*16-2*14','The first two scores total 28. All three must total 48, so the third score is 48 − 28 = 20.','Convert both averages to totals before subtracting.')
manipulation('ratio-transfer',1,'A box has 12 red and 20 blue tokens. How many blue tokens must be removed so that red and blue tokens are equally numerous?','4|8|12|16','8','20-12','Keep the 12 red tokens and reduce the blue count to 12. Remove 20 − 12 = 8 blue tokens.','Only the named group changes; do not split the difference between groups.')
manipulation('inverse-fraction-step',2,'After 6 is added to a number, the result is divided by 3 to give 11. What is the original number?','9|17|27|39','27','11*3-6','Before division the value was 11 × 3 = 33. Before adding 6 it was 33 − 6 = 27.','Undo the steps in reverse order.')
manipulation('unit-conversion-remainder',2,'A 2-metre cord is cut into five 30-cm lengths. How many centimetres remain?','20|30|50|150','50','2*100-5*30','Two metres is 200 cm. Five pieces use 150 cm, leaving 50 cm.','Convert to one unit before subtracting.')
manipulation('difference-of-squares',2,'How much greater is the square of 9 than the square of 7?','4|16|32|64','32','9**2-7**2','The squares are 81 and 49. Their difference is 32.','You can also use (9 − 7)(9 + 7) = 2 × 16.')
